{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_015","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Modify the settings or properties of an account in the XRP Ledger .","location_hint":"paragraph 227","char_start":4627,"char_end":4694,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_016","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"{\n\"TransactionType\" : \"AccountSet\" ,\n\"Account\" : \"rf1BiGeXwwQoi8Z2ueFYTEXSwuJYfV2Jpn\" ,\n\"Fee\" : \"12\" ,\n\"Sequence\" : 5 ,\n\"Domain\" : \"6578616D706C652E636F6D\" ,\n\"SetFlag\" : 5 ,\n\"MessageKey\" : \"03AB40A0490F9B7ED8DF29D246BF2D6269820A0EE7742ACDD457BEA7C7D0931EDB\"\n}","location_hint":"paragraph 229","char_start":4725,"char_end":4984,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_017","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"In addition to the common fields , AccountSet transactions use the following fields:","location_hint":"paragraph 232","char_start":5032,"char_end":5116,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_018","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Field JSON Type Internal Type Description","location_hint":"paragraph 233","char_start":5120,"char_end":5161,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_019","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"ClearFlag Number UInt32 Unique identifier of a flag to disable for this account.","location_hint":"paragraph 234","char_start":5165,"char_end":5245,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_020","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Domain String Blob The domain that owns this account, as a string of hex representing the ASCII for the domain in lowercase. Cannot be more than 256 bytes in length.","location_hint":"paragraph 235","char_start":5247,"char_end":5412,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_021","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"EmailHash String UInt128 An arbitrary 128-bit value. Conventionally, clients treat this as the md5 hash of an email address to use for displaying a Gravatar image.","location_hint":"paragraph 236","char_start":5414,"char_end":5577,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_022","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"MessageKey String Blob Public key for sending encrypted messages to this account. To set the key, it must be exactly 33 bytes, with the first byte indicating the key type: 0x02 or 0x03 for secp256k1 keys, 0xED for Ed25519 keys. To remove the key, use an empty value.","location_hint":"paragraph 237","char_start":5579,"char_end":5845,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_023","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"NFTokenMinter String - Address AccountID Another account that can mint NFTokens for you .","location_hint":"paragraph 238","char_start":5847,"char_end":5936,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_024","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Requires the NonFungibleTokensV1_1 amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 239","char_start":5938,"char_end":5995,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_025","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"SetFlag Number UInt32 Integer flag to enable for this account.","location_hint":"paragraph 240","char_start":5999,"char_end":6061,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_026","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"TransferRate Number UInt32 The fee to charge when users transfer this account&#x27;s tokens, represented as billionths of a unit. Cannot be more than 2000000000 or less than 1000000000 , except for the special case 0 meaning no fee.","location_hint":"paragraph 241","char_start":6063,"char_end":6295,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_027","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"TickSize Number UInt8 (Optional) Tick size to use for offers involving a currency issued by this address. The exchange rates of those offers is rounded to this many significant digits. Valid values are 3 to 15 inclusive, or 0 to disable.","location_hint":"paragraph 242","char_start":6297,"char_end":6534,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_028","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Requires the TickSize amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 243","char_start":6536,"char_end":6580,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_029","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"WalletLocator String UInt256 An arbitrary 256-bit value. If specified, the value is stored as part of the account but has no inherent meaning or requirements.","location_hint":"paragraph 244","char_start":6584,"char_end":6742,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_030","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"WalletSize Number UInt32 Not used. This field is valid in AccountSet transactions but does nothing.","location_hint":"paragraph 245","char_start":6744,"char_end":6843,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_031","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"If none of these options are provided, then the AccountSet transaction has no effect (beyond destroying the transaction cost). See Cancel or Skip a Transaction for more details.","location_hint":"paragraph 247","char_start":6875,"char_end":7052,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_032","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"The Domain field is represented as the hex string of the lowercase ASCII of the domain. For example, the domain example.com would be represented as \"6578616D706C652E636F6D\" .","location_hint":"paragraph 249","char_start":7062,"char_end":7236,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_033","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"To remove the Domain field from an account, send an AccountSet with the Domain set to an empty string.","location_hint":"paragraph 250","char_start":7238,"char_end":7340,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_034","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"You can put any domain in your account&#x27;s Domain field. To prove that an account and domain belong to the same person or business, you need a \"two-way link\":","location_hint":"paragraph 251","char_start":7342,"char_end":7503,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_035","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Accounts you own should have a domain you own in the Domain field.","location_hint":"paragraph 252","char_start":7507,"char_end":7573,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_036","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"At that domain, host an xrp-ledger.toml file listing accounts you own, and optionally other information about how you use the XRP Ledger.","location_hint":"paragraph 253","char_start":7575,"char_end":7712,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_037","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"There are several options which can be either enabled or disabled for an account. Account options are represented by different types of flags depending on the situation:","location_hint":"paragraph 255","char_start":7734,"char_end":7903,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_038","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"The AccountSet transaction type has several \"AccountSet Flags\" (prefixed asf ) that can enable an option when passed as the SetFlag parameter, or disable an option when passed as the ClearFlag parameter. Newer options have only this style of flag. You can enable up to one asf flag per transaction, and disable up to one asf flag per transaction.","location_hint":"paragraph 256","char_start":7907,"char_end":8253,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_039","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"The AccountSet transaction type has several transaction flags (prefixed tf ) that can be used to enable or disable specific account options when passed in the Flags parameter. You can enable and disable a combination of settings in one transaction using multiple tf flags, but not all settings have tf flags.","location_hint":"paragraph 257","char_start":8255,"char_end":8563,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_040","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"The AccountRoot ledger object type has several ledger-state-flags (prefixed lsf ) which represent the state of particular account options within a particular ledger. These settings apply until a transaction changes them.","location_hint":"paragraph 258","char_start":8565,"char_end":8785,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_041","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"To enable or disable Account Flags, use the SetFlag and ClearFlag parameters of an AccountSet transaction. AccountSet flags have names that begin with asf .","location_hint":"paragraph 259","char_start":8789,"char_end":8945,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_042","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"All flags are disabled by default.","location_hint":"paragraph 260","char_start":8947,"char_end":8981,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_043","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"The available AccountSet flags are:","location_hint":"paragraph 261","char_start":8983,"char_end":9018,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_044","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Flag Name Decimal Value Description","location_hint":"paragraph 262","char_start":9022,"char_end":9057,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_045","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"asfAccountTxnID 5 Track the ID of this account&#x27;s most recent transaction. Required for AccountTxnID","location_hint":"paragraph 263","char_start":9061,"char_end":9165,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_046","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"asfAllowTrustLineClawback 16 Allow account to claw back tokens it has issued. (Requires the Clawback amendment.) Can only be set if the account has an empty owner directory (no trust lines, offers, escrows, payment channels, checks, or signer lists). After you set this flag, it cannot be reverted. The account permanently gains the ability to claw back issued assets on trust lines.","location_hint":"paragraph 264","char_start":9167,"char_end":9550,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_047","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"asfAllowTrustLineLocking 17 Allow Trust Line tokens issued by this account to be held in escrow . If not enabled, tokens issued by this account can&#x27;t be escrowed. After you enable this flag, it cannot be disabled.","location_hint":"paragraph 265","char_start":9552,"char_end":9770,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_048","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Requires the TokenEscrow amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 266","char_start":9772,"char_end":9819,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_049","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"asfAuthorizedNFTokenMinter 10 Enable to allow another account to mint non-fungible tokens (NFTokens) on this account&#x27;s behalf. Specify the authorized account in the NFTokenMinter field of the AccountRoot object. To remove an authorized minter, enable this flag and omit the NFTokenMinter field.","location_hint":"paragraph 267","char_start":9823,"char_end":10122,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_050","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"Requires the NonFungibleTokensV1_1 amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 268","char_start":10124,"char_end":10181,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_097142ab08d3_051","source_id":"src_097142ab08d3","source_hash":"7451d4268f8c681081bc1fd8c4ca0b13d203a57018b7e284d69de39fd7df94fb","text":"asfDefaultRipple 8 Enable rippling on this account&#x27;s trust lines by default.","location_hint":"paragraph 269","char_start":10185,"char_end":10266,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:54:30.083Z"}
